WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.220
A friend tells you she
saw a dead man walk.

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.690
Should you believe her?

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.350
And what if many people said the same?

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:13.020
In 1748, the Scottish philosopher David
Hume asked how a wise person should weigh

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.640
reports like these.

6
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:19.320
So could any amount of eyewitness evidence
make it reasonable to believe a miracle

7
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.360
happened?

8
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:24.230
In this mission, you'll set
testimony against the laws of nature,

9
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.930
on a pair of scales.

10
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.350
Then you'll hear Richard Swinburne, a
philosopher who defends belief in miracles,

11
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.890
reply to Hume point by point.

12
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.180
Your mission: find out whether eyewitness
reports could ever make belief in a

13
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.530
miracle reasonable.
